{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035045-mage-the-ascension-if-was-an-anime","id":1035045,"title":"Mage the Ascension: If was an anime","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-19T20:57:18-08:00","id":1035045,"title":"Mage the Ascension: If was an anime","content":"So....i got a bunch of otakus/cosplayer players on my campaing. they are still getting a hold of the universe but they asked me to pitch some animes/mangas/videogames that might fit with different Traditions so they can get more proper examples and more precise characters within franchises as well.<br /> <br /> Could anyone help me fill this list?<br /> <br /> Euthanathos: im half picking Cowboy Bebop in here, Another , <br /> <br /> Verbena: Trigun? (I meant..vash could pass as one since he is a plant) , Black jack?<br /> <br /> Cult of Ectasy:<br /> <br /> Order of Hermes: Card Captors Sakura, Hellsing (the Hellsing organization), Im sorry...Bible Black (NSFW), Sailor Moon? , XXXHolic?<br /> <br /> Celestial Chorus:<br /> <br /> Akashic Brotherhood: JoJo Bizarre Adventures (Phantom Blood and Battle Tendencies) , One Punch Man? , Rurouni Kenshin<br /> <br /> Hollow Ones: Great Teacher Onizuka<br /> <br /> Dream Speakers : Shaman King, Lain, Chihiro's Journey and My Neighbourg totoro , Kitaro<br /> <br /> Virtual Adept: Digimon (season 1 and 2)<br /> <br /> Son of Aether: FLCL , Cyborg 009 <br /> <br /> Technocracy. Ghost in the Shell, PsychoPass, Lain, The Hastur organization from Digimon 3. Nerv from Evangelion, Monster , TerraFormers<br /> <br /> <br /> dunno where to fit Saint Seiya xD<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T21:55:12-08:00","id":1035066,"title":"","content":"&quot;Paprika&quot; for the Virtual Adepts. Arguably Persona 4 as well.<br /> <br /> Dragon Ball for the Akashic<br /> <br /> Kiki's Deliver Service could fit for Verbena.<br /> <br /> Code Gease for the Euthanatos perhaps (It's been a long time since I watched this one)<br /> <br /> You could arguably have Wolfwood from Trigun be in the Celestial Chorus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T22:34:22-08:00","id":1035082,"title":"","content":"Lain also works for Virtual Adepts. It's a versatile series.<br /> <br /> Akashayana: Hunter X Hunter<br /> <br /> Order of Hermes: Negima!, A Certain Magical Index, Full Metal Alchemist (one third of the Thrice-Great triumverant, after all, is Alchemy), maybe Madoka Magica (the Witches' names are rendered in Enochian script, and then there's the whole Faust angle)<br /> <br /> Society of Ether: Steamboy, Stein's Gate, Redline, Fraken Fran (Mature), a bit of Bleach (specifically the various mad scientist characters), Embalmed: The Another Tale Of Frankenstein [sic], Baccano!, The Big O, Jojo's Bizarre Adventure (Part 2), Read Or Die (the movie; less so the paper mastery, and more for the weird science on display)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T05:31:32-08:00","id":1035175,"title":"","content":"Where would Railgun fit from A Certain Scientific Railgun? I really do not think that she would be Order of Hermes (the series is the sequel to A Certain Magical Index), as there really does not seem to be anything Hermetic about her practice (for people unfamiliar with the series, Railgun is a master of electromagnetic forces capable of accelerating a coin to relativistic speeds).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T06:20:47-08:00","id":1035185,"title":"","content":"IIRC Index espers use a weird form of magic without realising (they think it's the power of SCIENCE) that mucks up attempts to use the 'verse's regular sort. Definitely a mage paradigm, definitely <i>not</i> Order of Hermes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T07:17:04-08:00","id":1035205,"title":"","content":"So good magey anime:<br /> <br /> <br /> Fate(various): You get alot of the feel if not the specifics of powers from it, not that an orphan couldn't get a solid paradigm just following the rules described there.<br /> <br /> Bakemonogatari: I am not sure I could name the traditions of the magicians as clearly as i could fate but the whole behind scenes world of belief and magic gives a solid Mood of Mage.<br /> <br /> The Eccentric Family: Normally I give this one for changeling but Benten is SO the Mage who decides to fuck around in another game. Plus you have all sorts of wierd superstions and the whole secret magical world.<br /> <br /> FlipFlappers: This might be a better &quot;Awakening&quot; series than Ascension since personal mind worlds aren't much of a thing in Ascension, still Mad Science being used to explore supposedly mystical worlds all being perfectly Sciencey.<br /> <br /> Izetta: For a more historical chronicle its pretty much what Czar Vargo did but from the Verbena/Hermetic perspective. And we see science try to conquer mysticism whether that's Etherite vs Technocrat welll..<br /> <br /> Mob psycho 100: Hubris and Humility along with alot of wierd custom powers and a secret occult world.<br /> <br /> Gachaman Crowds: the inversion of the Secret occult theme but shows the power of the masses when directed via social networking something that is readily the forte of the VA... and the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> I want to say shonen fighting anime for Akashics but honestly the majority I can think of basically give the Main character an explciitly special heretige which is fairly at odds with the conceit still hard work and training is one of their keys to their paradigm.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}